  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1203.79 Porous material",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1203.79 “Porous material” means a substance that has tiny openings, often microscopic, in which fluids may be absorbed or discharged, including but not limited to paper and corrugated paperboard. The term does not include wood.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-A 1200) #9933, eff 6-1-11; ss by #12899, eff 10-17-19",
